-                                       "ROOT MECHANISM 1 - the class library is missing exactly 7 expressible tokens: category-excludes.json already owns this failure class (its note: single source of truth for wrong-class product tokens) and its beverage class even lists tea in the EXEMPT regex, yet no class carries a tea / coffee / v8 / marshmallow / rice-cake / tampon / lip-balm token. audit-food-category (the blocking cell guard) reads the same library, so it is structurally blind to all 7 of these estate-wide today.",
-                                       "ROOT MECHANISM 2 - THE BAKE HAS DRIFTED 2,165 PATTERNS BEHIND THE LIBRARY: apply-category-excludes.ps1 -WhatIf (read-only, run by the reviewer) reports +2165 patterns across 443 commodities. The library grew (snack_carrier gained jerky, crisps, crackers tokens and more) but the bake was never re-run, so the garlic exclude list still predates snack_carrier entirely - which is exactly why Krave Beef Jerky could reach garlic even though the library already knows jerky is wrong on every Fruit/Vegetables commodity. The workflow doc says register -\u003e apply -\u003e compare; nothing enforces the apply step and no guard watches bake currency. This is the job-whose-cadence-cannot-keep-up shape.",
-                                       "ROOT MECHANISM 3 - category scoping holes: milk (Dairy \u0026 Eggs), rice (Pasta), chocolate-chips (Baking), bagels (Bread), honey and peanuts (Coffee, Oils \u0026 Spreads), canned-black-beans (Canned), bacon (Meat) receive only babyfood/pet/household/supplement classes from the apply rules, so bakery/dairy/snack tokens can never reach them via the library. Those routes need per-commodity tokens (the library\u0027s own rule: anything item-specific stays in the commodity\u0027s exclude list).",
