-                      "root_cause":  "First-match-wins can only be as good as the exclude walls, and three separate mechanisms had holes: (a) seven wrong-product classes the library cannot express today (tea, coffee, v8, marshmallow, rice-cake, tampon, lip-balm) - so neither the baked excludes NOR the blocking audit-food-category guard can see them anywhere in the estate; (b) the bake step is manual and has silently drifted 2,165 patterns behind the library across 443 commodities, so even tokens the library HAS (jerky) protect nothing - jerky-on-garlic is purely this; (c) category scoping does not give dairy/bread/baking/pasta/canned/meat commodities the bakery/dairy/snack classes, so those misroutes need per-commodity tokens, which nobody had written because nothing surfaces a CANDIDATE-level wrong product until it is one sale from a cell (match-soundness flags them as contested, but the round-1 review checked each commodity crown instead of each product routing - the process gap the bounce correctly named). The bounce\u0027s other premise - missing sanity bands - is measured FALSE: all 21 involved commodities are banded and the bands demonstrably fired (candidates-2026-07-30 OUT-OF-BAND stamps on the exact rows); bands are also the wrong tool, because a 0.22/oz marshmallow is inside any band that still admits the real 0.2494 Hy-Vee strawberries. STRUCTURAL ANSWER TO THE DISPATCH QUESTION: the right fix is routing repair through the designed library + re-bake + measured commodity tokens (option a, done properly through the library); NOT option b new bands (nothing to add - the set is fully banded and bands cannot separate in-band wrong products); NOT option d leave-it (the marshmallow already outprices two real strawberry rows and the tea is one 21-cent price move from the lemons crown).",
