-                      "deviation":  "SHIPPED, and the frozen 130-name contract REPRODUCED before anything was accepted. Method: a read-only routing snapshot (engine-faithful replica, assign-then-wrap everywhere) over 25,939 distinct names / 22,467 in-feed across 113 capture files, taken BEFORE and AFTER the change and diffed against expected_routing_changes. Result: 131 names changed routing, of which 128 are the contract verbatim. Every one of the 130 contract lines fired; none went missing. audit-match-soundness independently reported MOVED=63 DROPPED=47 with drift-vs-engine=0, which reconciles to the same three-line delta below, and after -Accept it reports 0/0/0.\n\nTHREE MEASURED DIFFERENCES FROM THE PLAN, all of them the plan\u0027s own intent, none a new mechanism:\n(1) \u0027La Costena Black Beans, Refried 20.5 Oz\u0027 and \u0027La Preferida Black Beans, Refried 16 Oz\u0027 land in REFRIED-BEANS, not \u003cunmatched\u003e as the frozen list says. That is what the plan\u0027s own new include \u0027black\\s+beans,?\\s+refried\u0027 does - the comma form matches it. Verified by rule replay before the edit (include hit, no exclude hit, no GLOBAL_EXCLUDE hit) and confirmed live. Better than the contract: two real refried-bean cans get their correct owner instead of being dropped. They lose there to Casa Mamita 0.0619, so no cell moved.\n(2) \u0027Ranch Style Beans with Sliced Jalapeno Peppers\u0027 -\u003e \u003cunmatched\u003e is the ONE changed name absent from expected_routing_changes - and it is the plan\u0027s own found-while-measuring correction, carried in its evidence, its change_tokens (pickled-jalapenos exclude \\bbeans\\b) and its expected_cell_changes. Only the routing line was missing from the frozen list.\n(3) The bake reported +3687 patterns across 445 commodities, not the plan\u0027s \"roughly +2170 across roughly 443\". The plan\u0027s estimate counted the pre-existing drift (measured here at exactly +2165 across 443 before any edit, as predicted) but not the fan-out of the SEVEN NEW library tokens across the scoped categories (household x2 reaches every scoped commodity, beverage x3 reaches Fruit/Vegetables/Meat, candy and snack_carrier reach Fruit/Vegetables). A pattern-count estimate, not a behavioural difference: the behaviour is the 130-name diff, and that reproduced.\n\nBOARD DIFF, 2833 cells before and after: ZERO cells lost, ZERO added, 8 changed. THREE are the plan\u0027s expected corrections to the cent - mixed-nuts @ Walmart 0.3675 -\u003e 0.3548 (crown flips Aldi -\u003e Walmart), mixed-nuts @ Baker\u0027s 0.4359 -\u003e 0.4279, pickled-jalapenos @ Baker\u0027s 0.0833 -\u003e 0.1139 (the bean can out, La Costena Sliced Jalapeno Peppers 28 oz in, price RISES because the wrong cheap product left). The FOURTH expected change was a non-change by design and verified as such: mixed-nuts @ Aldi holds 0.3654 on the renamed Southern Grove row, so the cell survives the store rename instead of dying when the old-name capture ages out.\nFIVE CELL CHANGES BEYOND expected_cell_changes, each adjudicated against the candidate rows rather than assumed:\n  - FOUR are same-price tie reshuffles with ZERO price movement, caused by contract arrivals joining an existing tie: breakfast-sandwiches @ Baker\u0027s (4 products all at 1.3738, Kroger Bacon Egg and Cheese Croissant arrived), canned-black-beans @ Walmart (3 Great Value black bean SKUs all at 0.0573, the refried rows left), iced-tea @ Baker\u0027s (4 Kroger gallon teas all at 0.0257, AriZona Lemon Iced Tea arrived), refried-beans @ Baker\u0027s (5 Kroger refried SKUs all at 0.0744, Simple Truth Organic Fat Free Refried Black Beans arrived). Every replacement is a legitimate member of its commodity at the identical per-unit price; no published number moved.\n  - ONE is a real correction the plan did not propagate to its cell list: rice-cakes @ Family Fare 0.6487 -\u003e 0.5662, because \u0027Quaker Caramel Chocolate Chip Rice Cakes 7.4 Oz\u0027 ($4.19 / 7.4 oz) left chocolate-chips (a contract line) and is genuinely the cheapest Family Fare rice cake. The cell gets cheaper because a real product arrived in its correct commodity.\n\nSTEP 9 (pre-ack the 3 expected_new_review_flags) NOT DONE, and deliberately: there is no such thing as an ack key for an out-of-band drop. check-ad-cycles builds review-flag keys in exactly four namespaces (SANITY|commodity|type from guards-\u003cdate\u003e.json, MULTIBUY|store|id, BASIS|id|store, PACKBASIS|id|store); band drops are logged to flagged-\u003cdate\u003e.json and never page, and review-ack.json\u0027s own how_to_ack says to use \"the flag key from out\\alerted-flags.json\". Three invented keys would suppress nothing and would put unverifiable rows in the one file whose value is that every row is a real reviewed suppression. Measured instead: re-running sanity-check.ps1 on the new board gives 48 flags before and 48 after, ZERO new, ZERO cleared, ZERO changed details - this change created no pageable review flag at all. All three arrivals ARE out-of-band exactly as predicted and can never publish (beef-jerky Krave 3.5667 vs max 3; crackers Blue Diamond Nut-Thins 0.9388 vs max 0.6; sandwich-cookies Milano Baker\u0027s 6 oz 0.8317 vs max 0.6), verified in flagged-2026-07-31.json.\n\nPROOF THE NEW WATCHERS CAN ACTUALLY FIRE (the 2026-07-29 reachable-self-test lesson): both new cases were run against a negative control, not just observed green. (a) The three frozen food-category rows were replayed against the PRE-CHANGE library in an isolated copy: \"ok - no food commodity matched a wrong-class product (3 priced cells scanned)\", exit 0 - the exact blindness the plan describes. Against the shipped library all three hard-fail (exit 2) and name household / candy / beverage. (b) The bake-currency must-fire fixture reports \"+2 patterns across 1 commodities\"; with the ^apples$ exempt removed from a TEMP copy it reports \"+4 patterns across 2 commodities\", so the shipped assertion is load-