-    "open_questions_for_brad":  [
-                                    "ANSWERED BY BRAD 2026-07-31 AND SHIPPED - see brad_decision_shipped below. ORIGINAL QUESTION: taco-sauce commodity meaning: Sam\u0027s carries \u0027Taco Bell Mild Sauce, 25 oz.\u0027 at $4.98 - genuinely taco sauce, but any include token that admits it also admits Taco Bell Fire/Diablo/Hot Sauce bottles at Baker\u0027s and Walmart (~21 Taco Bell products estate-wide, measured). Should taco-sauce include Taco Bell restaurant-style bottles (all heat levels), only Mild/Original, or stay as-is? Allowlisted as a reviewed gap until you call it. BRAD RULED: the restaurant-style Taco Bell sauce BOTTLES are taco sauce at ALL FOUR heat levels (Mild, Hot, Fire, Diablo). taco-sauce stays a SAUCE commodity: the seasoning mixes and shakers, the Mild Salsa Con Queso cheese dip and the Verde Salsa bottle are NOT taco sauce and keep being rejected. Implemented, gated and published the same day, and the coverage-gap allowlist entry that parked this question was deleted so a future taco-sauce gap surfaces as a real gap instead of staying hidden."
-                                ],
-    "brad_decision_shipped":  {
-                                  "question":  "taco-sauce commodity meaning - the only entry in open_questions_for_brad",
-                                  "ruled_by":  "Brad",
-                                  "ruled_on":  "2026-07-31",
-                                  "decision":  "The Taco Bell restaurant-style sauce BOTTLES belong to taco-sauce at ALL heat levels: Mild, Hot, Fire and Diablo. taco-sauce remains a sauce commodity, so the Taco Bell seasoning mixes and shakers, the Mild Salsa Con Queso cheese dip and the Verde Salsa bottle are NOT taco sauce and must keep being rejected.",
-                                  "why_recorded_here":  "commodities.json has no comment or note convention anywhere in its 503 entries and is rewritten wholesale by apply-category-excludes.ps1, so a rationale placed there would be both unprecedented and fragile. The plan file is the estate's committed home for rule reasoning and it ships in the same commit as the rule.",
-                                  "rules_changed":  [
-                                                        "grocery/commodities.json - taco-sauce.include gains the token Brad measured: taco backslash-s-plus bell backslash-s-plus (mild|hot|fire|diablo|verde|salsa backslash-s-plus verde) optional backslash-s-star sauce",
-                                                        "grocery/commodities.json - hot-sauce.exclude gains 'taco backslash-s-plus bell'. THIS IS THE DEVIATION; without it the Hot bottle can never reach taco-sauce.",
-                                                        "grocery/coverage-gap-allowlist.json - the taco-sauce @ Sam's Club PARKED FOR BRAD entry deleted, 194 entries down to 193"
